   "title": "Instruction (sees Picture 1 + 2)",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Transform the storyboard in Picture 1 into a finished film frame. Preserve its crop, subject scale, viewpoint, poses and the number and placement of characters and props. Create this shot in the specific location described below: medium close-up from the chest up. Visible first frame: Close on his hands turning the glowing lens; light fractures into rainbows across his face. Location context: The city drifts above a sea of ochre sand, structures of blown, iridescent glass clinging to massive, slow-moving buoyancy platforms. Use the location and atmosphere; do not add offscreen characters or actions from this description. Picture 1 is the storyboard drawing of this shot: use its composition, camera angle, framing, where the characters are placed and how they pose, but render a real photographic film frame in full colour using the specified film look and lighting; nothing pencil-drawn or sketched. Keep the storyboard's camera view, crop and subject placement. Preserve any sketched scenery; complete a plain or incomplete background using the location context without adding a wide establishing view. The lead is the character from Picture 2 with the same species, face, distinctive markings, colouring, build and wardrobe. Picture 2 is only an identity reference: take their pose, expression and body language from this shot's action, not from Picture 2, and play it with the emotion the moment calls for. Ignore the studio backdrop of Picture 2. The lead is the only character in the frame. The lead: Medium brown skin, oval face with defined jawline, dark brown eyes, black braids, early 20s, slender build. Thin build, indigo linen, dark braids, glowing crucible. Same color grade: golden hour backlight, warm sun flare, long shadows, dreamy atmosphere. Cinematic still frame from a live-action feature film: realistic light, natural colour and texture, no text, no borders."
   ]
  },
